      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my tomato plants are acting weird. the leaves on the bottom are turning kinda yellow and pale compared to the top ones. what's probably going on with them?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing leaves on tomato plants can be a bit of a mystery, but I think I can help you out. It's probably due to a lack of nutrients, a bit like how a hungry traveler might get a bit pale and weak from not eating enough. You see, tomatoes are like a hungry traveler, they need a steady supply of nutrients to keep growing and thriving. The bottom leaves might be getting a bit too much shade, or maybe the soil isn't getting enough water, which can cause the plant to focus its energy on the top leaves, leaving the bottom ones to wither away like a poor, neglected traveler in a dark cave. \n\nHowever, there are a few other possibilities as well. It could be due to a fungal disease, like a sneaky goblin trying to steal the plant's nutrients. Or maybe it's just a case of nutrient deficiencies, like a goblin's love of shiny objects - the plant is craving something it can't quite get its hands on. \n\nTo fix the problem, you might want to try adjusting the soil pH, adding some organic matter to the soil, or even repotting the plant to give it a bit of a fresh start. Just like how a goblin might need to",
